 seeks reelection in a Colorado district that leans Republican by about nine points, facing Democratic challenger Eileen Laubacher. Expert raters mostly place the race at Lean or Likely Republican, though two outlets call it a Tossup, and prediction markets give Boebert roughly a 70% chance. The only public poll, from September, showed Boebert ahead by five points among likely voters.\n\nThe most striking feature is money: Laubacher has raised over $13.7 million to Boebert's $1.2 million, giving the challenger a large cash-on-hand edge, though Boebert benefits from outside support. Boebert's polarizing profile and a contentious lone debate keep Democratic hopes alive, but the district's partisan lean remains the dominant force, pointing to a Republican favorite with real, if limited, upside for an upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2626, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.23, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2767, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3037, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.297, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2256, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2601, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2778, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2282, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2266, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0